{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791667502,"nonce":"QGyStEn92gyC0b9ASRthrCrq4zY=","title":"Pointer and anchor positions ignored the scroll of the containers around a control","message":"A press in a text area, a drag on a vertical range, and a select's list placement compared window coordinates with layout bounds, which do not include what a scrolled container has moved.\n\nReproduced: a text area inside a container scrolled by 298 px, pressed on its third line, put the caret on the first line (index 1 of 38); the same press in an unscrolled container gave the right place. The range and the select list read bounds() the same way.\n\nFix: HostNode.viewBounds() is the layout bounds less the scroll of every composed ancestor (owned parts too, which are not in parentNode). Text fields, ranges and anchored placement read it. tests/native-view-bounds.mjs puts the same controls in a scrolled and an unscrolled container and requires the same result; each use fails it when put back to bounds().\n\nNot covered: position: fixed content inside a scroller, which would not scroll with it.","files":null}]}